  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 5603.02 Form for Certificate of Authority for Agents or Employees",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5603.02 Form for Certificate of Authority for Agents or Employees.\n\n(a) The certificate of authority for agents shall be:\n\n(1) On the principal's letterhead;\n\n(2) Indicate the name of the agent or employee;\n\n(3) If the agent is a corporation, partnership, or other legal entity, the letter shall indicate the name(s) of the individuals from the agent-entity authorized to receive records for the agent;\n\n(4) The period of time the authorization is valid for, but not to exceed one year; and\n\n(5) Signature of the principal, or if a legal entity, signature of the director, officer, or branch manager for the principal.\n\n(b) Notwithstanding any rule to the contrary, for the purposes of RSA 260:14, V(a), a certificate of authority shall be provided for each request for a motor vehicle record of a named person. Bulk users authorized by Saf-C 5602.08(a), however, do not need to submit a certificate of authority for each request.\n\nSource. #6403, EXEMPT, eff 1-1-97; rpld and ss by #7361, EXEMPT, eff 9-1-00; ss by #7621, EXEMPT, eff 1-1-02; ss by #13152, EXEMPT, eff 12-31-20",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c5600.html"
}
